      "description": "Watch Villarreal vs Levante highlights and goals from La Liga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 20, 2026. On September 20, 2026 , two Spanish rivals met in a crucial La Liga clash, with both sides seeking to establish their momentum in the league. The atmosphere was electric from the first whistle, promising a contest filled with technical quality and tactical intrigue. First Half Drama and a Wondergoal The match began with Villarreal asserting their dominance, pressing high and forcing the Levante defense into several early clearances. As early as the 4th minute, Ayoze Perez came agonizingly close to the opener, only to see his goal-bound effort hacked off the line. The physical nature of the game was apparent from the start, with Aissa Mandi picking up an early yellow card for a rough challenge. After a period of sustained pressure, the deadlock was finally broken in the 41st minute. Alberto Moleiro turned provider, finding Ayoze Perez , who clinically finished with his right foot to give the hosts a 1-0 lead. However, the celebrations were short-lived as Levante produced a moment of absolute brilliance just a minute later. Following a precise cross from Jeremy Toljan , Ivan Romero connected with a stunning bicycle kick that flew into the net, leveling the score at 1-1. The equalizer stunned the home crowd and sent the teams into the tunnel at halftime with everything to play for, though the tension was visible as Luis Castro received a booking for dissent during the stoppage time. Moleiro Restores the Lead Villarreal returned for the second half with renewed focus, looking to reclaim their advantage. Their persistence paid off in the 54th minute when a defensive lapse by Jeremy Toljan allowed Pape Gueye and Ilias Akhomach to combine, setting up Alberto Moleiro . The playmaker showed great composure to slot the ball home with his left foot, making it 2-1. Following the goal, both managers turned to their benches, with Villarreal introducing Gerard no and Georges Mikautadze to maintain their offensive threat. As the clock ticked down, Levante struggled to find a way through a disciplined Villarreal backline. Peter Gulacsi and Renato Veiga remained alert to snuff out any potential danger from crosses. The match entered a cagey phase, marked by a tactical foul from Tajon Buchanan that earned him a yellow card as he stopped a budding Levante counter-attack. Mikautadze Puts it Beyond Doubt In the 86th minute, the home side effectively ended the contest. Exploiting another error in the Levante defense—this time from Jon Olasagasti — Alberto Moleiro recorded his second assist of the day by teeing up Georges Mikautadze . The substitute made no mistake, firing a left-footed shot into the corner to extend the lead to 3-1. Despite a late scare from a Yanis Musuayi header that went wide in the dying moments, the hosts held firm. With 63% possession and a clinical display in front of goal, Villarreal secured a deserved three points. The victory highlights their tactical maturity and ability to respond to adversity, keeping them on track in the La Liga standings."
